+# MASTER7 v153 provider catalogue safety release
+
+Release: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.153-provider-catalogue-safety`
+
+This release closes catalogue-boundary and reporting gaps across EPICWIN,
+META GAMING, JDB and JILI.
+
+- EPICWIN Normal MYR and Free MYR use independent request paths, cache keys,
+  profile identities, account checks and currency checks.
+- EPICWIN rejects malformed, duplicate and oversized catalogues as one unit.
+  Unknown per-title availability remains maintenance and remote artwork is not
+  exposed.
+- META GAMING retains isolated Normal and Free Credit profiles. Unknown title
+  availability remains suspended and unapproved artwork is withheld.
+- JDB defaults a missing availability field to maintenance and withholds
+  unapproved artwork.
+- JILI's two implemented adapters are reported as awaiting their incomplete
+  provider contract and production acceptance, rather than unimplemented.
+
+Current supplier evidence remains blocked: META GAMING and EPICWIN return HTTP
+403, while JDB returns provider status `9001`. The portal therefore exposes no
+Play action for these profiles. No player, launch, wallet, transfer, settlement
+or recovery request was added or enabled.
+
+VPay, GSPAY, 1MPay, payment switches, credentials, service plans and DNS are
+unchanged.
